# Kingsrest Isle - a new island of the library (ROADMAP 3d NI8), large, with no quest
# A big green island of hills. On a hill in the west stands a castle's ruin: a ring of crumbled stone walls with four
# stubby towers and a gate to the south, a ramp climbing to it, the lord's wooden hall and a well in the courtyard. In the
# south-east lies a village of thatched huts round a fire, a well and a tiki pole. In the north two rocky peaks hold the
# island's holy places - a wooden idol between fire baskets on the west peak, a ring of marble columns round a statue
# on the east one - and a rope bridge hangs between them; the east peak is reached only over it. Monsters: a bear in
# the north woods, warthogs in the south, screechers round the peaks.
#
# Built by the recipe player (CIRecipe kingsrest_isle) through the editor's own operations. Points: the castle hill at
# -40 10 (12 m, r 18), its walls at r 13, the gate south at -40 -3, the ramp from -40 -30 (3 m) to -40 -6 (12 m); the
# hall x -43.75..-36.25, z 9..13.5 (floor 12.1 m, door south); the village at 35 -40 (3 m, r 18), four huts along z
# -36..-33 from x 24 to 48, the fire at 35 -44; the west peak's top at 6 40 and the east peak's at 36 40 (both 22 m, r 10);
# the path up the west peak from 6 -6 (4 m) to 6 31; the bridge from 13.5 40 to 28.5 40 (deck 22 m, sagging 1.5 m).
include lib_huts
include lib_sea
include lib_features
include lib_ni34
include lib_ni8
new
# (nature: tropical, Like Raft - palms and bushes, the peaks bare rock)
gen Trees=0.28 Bushes=0.28 Rocks=0.43 Harvest=0.24 BeachThings=0.3
gen Seed=7803 Radius=90 Height=12 Roughness=0.4 Peaks=2 Shape=0 Style=0 BeachWidth=0.5 Cliffs=0.35 PeakShape=0.45
gen Water=0.5 SeaRocks=0.5 SeaFinds=0.3 Sunken=0.3 Hostiles=0 Friendly=0 SeaLife=0
generate

# ===== The ground: the castle hill and its ramp, the village, the two peaks, the saddle, the path up the west peak ======
brush flatten at -40 10 r=18 s=20 frames=220 h=12
for i 0 24 1
brush flatten at -40 {-30+$i} r=2.8 s=20 frames=30 h={3+$i*9/24}
next
brush smooth at -40 10 r=22 s=5 frames=30
brush grass at -40 10 r=12 s=10 frames=20
brush rock at -40 10 r=18 s=6 frames=20
brush flatten at 35 -40 r=18 s=20 frames=120 h=3
# (level pads for the two wells: their decks rest flat on the ground, the pipe buried)
brush flatten at -33 3 r=4.5 s=20 frames=150 h=11.9
brush flatten at 46 -46 r=4.5 s=20 frames=150 h=3.1
brush grass at 35 -40 r=16 s=10 frames=20
brush sand at 35 -44 r=5 s=20 frames=20
brush flatten from 19.5 40 to 22.5 40 r=3 s=20 frames=200 h=10
brush flatten at 6 40 r=10 s=20 frames=300 h=22
brush flatten at 36 40 r=10 s=20 frames=300 h=22
# (the path: two passes of strokes 1 m apart, on into the peak's top; no smoothing - on this narrow ridge a smooth
# stroke pulled it 5 m under its heights and left a wall at z 29-33)
for pp 1 2 1
for i 0 37 1
brush flatten at 6 {-6+$i} r=3.2 s=20 frames=120 h={4+$i*18/37}
next
brush flatten from 6 31 to 6 35 r=3.2 s=20 frames=120 h=22
next
brush rock at 6 40 r=11 s=20 frames=40
brush rock at 36 40 r=11 s=20 frames=40
clear at -40 10 r=18
clear from -40 -30 to -40 -5 r=3.5
clear at 35 -40 r=18
clear at 6 40 r=10
clear at 36 40 r=10
clear from 6 -9 to 6 34 r=4.5

# ===== The castle: the ring of crumbled walls with the gate south, four stubby towers, fire baskets at the gate =========
# (straight stone blocks with a flat foot, sunk 2 m or more under the lowest ground of their footprint, outer slope
# included - the boulder bulges of the first build read as rocks hovering over the slope; walls 10.2 m close the ring)
for wi 0 6 1
set wa {315+45*$wi}
place RT_GroundPillar castlewall at {-40+13*cos($wa)} {10+13*sin($wa)} h=7.4 sit yaw={atan2(-sin($wa),cos($wa))} sx=0.75 sy={(9.2+0.8*abs(sin($wa*3)))/3} sz=4.25
next
for a 45 315 90
place RT_GroundPillar castletower at {-40+13.5*cos($a)} {10+13.5*sin($a)} h=7.3 sit sx=1.58 sy=4.33 sz=1.58
next
place Placeable_Lantern_FireBasket - at -43 -4.5 ground sit
place Placeable_Lantern_FireBasket - at -37 -4.5 ground sit
place Note_Sign gatesign at -44 -7 ground yaw=180

# ===== The lord's hall in the courtyard: a wooden cabin, door south; his table, book and chest; the well ================
push at -43.75 9 h=12
call cabin w=5 d=3 al=hallwall
place Placeable_Table_Basic - at 3.75 2.6 y=0.1 sit
place Note_Book lordsbook at 3.75 2.6 y=0.84 sit yaw=20
place Loot_Chest lordschest at 6.6 3.6 y=0.1 sit yaw=270
place Placeable_Bed_Basic - at 1.15 3 y=0.1 sit yaw=90
pop
place Well - at -33 3 ground y=-1.8 sit
place Loot_Barrel castlebarrel at -48 4 ground

# ===== The village in the south-east: four thatched huts, the fire, a tiki pole, the well, a barrel ====================
for hx 24 43.5 6.5
push at $hx -36 h=3
call ni8hut w=3 d=2 al=huts
pop
next
place Loot_Chest headmanchest at 34.2 -33.8 h=3.1 sit yaw=180
place campfire_1 - at 35 -44 ground
place Placeable_TikiPole_Complete - at 30 -46 ground sit yaw=10
place Placeable_TikiPole_Complete - at 40 -46 ground sit yaw=350
place Well - at 46 -46 ground y=-1.8 sit
place Loot_Barrel villagebarrel at 23 -42 ground
line Block_Wall_Fence_Plank from 22 -50 to 30 -50 step=1.5 ground
place Note_Paper villagenote at 33 -43 ground sit yaw=30

# ===== The holy places on the peaks: the idol on the west peak, the column ring round the statue on the east; the bridge =
place Balboa_DecorationPrefabBase_Doll_R idol at 4 42 ground sit scale=2.4 yaw=180
place Placeable_Lantern_FireBasket - at 2.4 42 ground sit
place Placeable_Lantern_FireBasket - at 5.6 42 ground sit
place Note_Sign peaksign at 9 37 ground yaw=270
call ni8temple x=36 z=40 h=22 al=templecolumns roofal=templeroof
# (the slab's corners stand out past the ring: a post under each, so the roof rests on posts at its corners too)
for cx -1 1 2
for cz -1 1 2
place RT_PillarThick templecolumns at {36+4.2*$cx} {40+4.2*$cz} h=22 sy=0.483 sx=0.3 sz=0.3
next
next
prop templecolumns tint.color=#e8e2d4
prop templeroof tint.color=#e8e2d4
place TangaroaFounderStatue statue at 36 40 h=22 sit scale=0.55 yaw=270
place UT_EndRoom_Pot02 - at 34 42.5 h=22 sit
place Loot_Chest offeringchest at 37.5 37.6 h=22 sit yaw=270
call ni8air x=36 z=40 h=23 al=templeair fog=#d8d8e8 fa=0.1 light=#fff4d0 la=0.25 parts=mist r=8
call hangbridge x1=13.5 z1=40 h1=22 x2=28.5 z2=40 h2=22 sag=1.5 pb=2

# ===== The sea: Raft's finds in the shallows, dolphins ===================================================================
call shallows r=105 deep=5 n=1 seed=7850
place Creature_Dolphin dolphins at 70 -80 h=-3

# ===== Monsters: a bear in the north woods, warthogs in the south, screechers round the peaks ===========================
place Creature_Bear bear at -25 55 ground
place Creature_Boar hogs at -5 -55 ground
place Creature_StoneBird screechers at 21 40 h=34

# ===== Raft's features: wild bees, dirt, a buried tin, a chest under vines ==============================================
call hives x=-10 z=-20 r=24 n=3 seed=7851
call dirt x=10 z=-30 r=20 n=4 seed=7852
call treasure x=60 z=20 r=14 n=1 seed=7853
call vinecache x=-60 z=-40 r=14 seed=7854 items=Rope*3;Nail*10;CopperOre*2

# ===== Settings, notes, loot (no quest) ===================================================================================
info title=Kingsrest Isle
info author=Custom Islands
info description=A big green island with a ruined castle on its west hill, a village of thatched huts, an idol and a ring of marble columns on two rocky peaks and a rope bridge hanging between them. A bear, warthogs and screechers. No quest.

note gatesign Stone by the gate | KINGSREST\nThe king's peace holds inside these walls.\nThe walls have not held for a long time.
note lordsbook The lord's book | KINGSREST\n\nThe last of the masons left with the spring boats. The towers will not go higher now.\nThe village keeps the fire and the old idol on the west peak. I keep the hall.\nWe hung a bridge to the east peak where the white stones stand. One crossing at a time.\nThe bear in the north woods is older than the castle. Leave him be.
note lordschest The lord's chest | The lord's chest: iron, leather, a little copper, his good rope.
loot lordschest MetalIngot*2;Leather*3;CopperIngot*1;Rope*3
prop lordschest loot.refill=0
note castlebarrel Barrel in the courtyard | A barrel in the courtyard: planks, nails, stone.
loot castlebarrel Plank*4;Nail*8;Stone*4
prop castlebarrel loot.refill=0
note villagenote The villagers' notice | Fire at dusk. Water from the well, not the sea.\nGifts for the white stones go over the bridge. Nobody takes them back.\nThe pigs in the south woods bite.
note headmanchest Headman's chest | The headman's chest: seeds, bait, wool, a sweep net.
loot headmanchest Seed_Mango*2;FishingBait_Simple*3;Wool*2;SweepNet*1
prop headmanchest loot.refill=0
note villagebarrel Barrel in the village | A barrel by the huts: clay, sand, plastic.
loot villagebarrel Clay*3;Sand*3;Plastic*3
prop villagebarrel loot.refill=0
note peaksign Sign by the idol | THE CROSSING TO THE WHITE STONES\nOne at a time.
note offeringchest Offering chest | Gifts left for the white stones: titanium, silver algae, copper, honey.
loot offeringchest TitaniumOre*2;SilverAlgae*2;CopperIngot*2;HoneyComb*2
prop offeringchest loot.refill=0
prop hogs creature.count=2
prop screechers creature.count=2
prop dolphins creature.count=2

posts off
save Kingsrest Isle
